# A .gitignore file is literally just a list of files/folders that Git should pretend don't exist.

## Python generated files

# When Python runs your code, it sometimes automatically creates a folder called: __pycache__
# containing little compiled versions of Python files that help Python run/import things efficiently.
__pycache__/

# this means: Ignore any file ending in .pyc.
# (The * means anything)
# .pyc files are also automatically generated compiled Python files.
*.pyc

## Virtual environment

# In extremely simplified terms, it's a private little Python setup specifically for Girlie Computer.
# That .venv folder can contain thousands of files.
# We absolutely don't want Git uploading all of those. Instead, GitHub will eventually have a small file saying essentially:
# "Girlie Computer requires PySide6 version X, Pygame version Y..."

Then another computer can install those packages itself.
.venv/

# Girlie Computer's personal database
# That actual file contains your data.
*.db

## Environment/secrets

# Sometimes programs need secret information — API keys, passwords/tokens, configuration that shouldn't be public, etc.
# A common place to keep those locally is: .env

notes.txt